# The programs tests/faster-rows compiles twice, by the shipped frontend
# and by the one built without its Faster rows, each with the rows it
# reaches. A Faster row on Nat's arithmetic is reached only with naturals
# a unary count computes in the test's limits: the program tests of large
# naturals (nat-sum, nat-parity) would run past them from the bodies,
# which is speed, and no result.
program char-list-pipeline   base's list as the string builders take it apart; pack, unpack
program exit-with            exitWith
program identity-weakening   finToNat and natToFinLT, the identity on a natural
program erased-argument-to-a-variable   show of a small natural through natToInteger
program every-builtin-export   rewrite__impl and replace, the identity on their last argument
reject uniqueness-shared-rebuild   an in-place type, a Stricter row, over the list functions
reject deprecated-get-byte   a deprecated name, a Stricter row
reject polymorphism-growing-rank   a refusal of the frontend's own analysis, no row's
